# Operator clear of the whole-drive fault -- SR-18 amendment 2026-11-09.
#
# Served by swerve_controller on /swerve_controller/clear_drive_fault.
# Accepted ONLY while a whole-drive fault is latched AND its reason is one of
# STALL_RETRIP, STALL_TRIP_COUNT, STALL_MULTI_WHEEL, STALL_LATCHED_HELD
# (DriveFault REASON_* codes 2, 3, 4, 5). ENCODER_MISSING and FEEDBACK_LOST
# are refused: they need a stack restart (Mode R or a bringup service start).
#
# A CLEAR IS A MOTION RELEASE. There is no precondition (user decision D2): a
# drive command that is still held at clear time makes the robot drive off at
# once. The only protection afterwards is the re-armed detection.
#
# success = true is returned only after the controller's update loop has
# applied the clear (latch released, marker removed, detection re-armed).
# On any failure nothing changes and the fault stays latched, in memory and in
# the crash-surviving marker.
#
# ROS services carry no authenticated caller identity: `requester` is what the
# caller claims (e.g. "web_teleop", "cli"); empty is logged as "unspecified".
#
# CLI (one line):
#   ros2 service call /swerve_controller/clear_drive_fault
#   gripperx_control_msgs/srv/ClearDriveFault
#   "{requester: 'cli', expected_reason: 0, expected_fault_id: 0}"

string requester
# DriveFault REASON_* the caller believes is latched; 0 = no expectation. A
# non-zero value that differs from the latched reason is refused (protects a
# dialog that is showing a stale fault).
uint8 expected_reason
# DriveFault.fault_id of the fault the caller reviewed. Non-zero and different
# from the latched fault's id -> refused ("fault changed, review again"), so a
# dialog can never clear a fault it did not show. 0 = no expectation (CLI
# convenience; the caller then clears whatever STALL_* fault is latched).
# CLI with the check: read fault_id first, e.g.
#   ros2 topic echo --once --qos-durability transient_local
#   --qos-reliability reliable /swerve_controller/drive_fault
# and pass it as expected_fault_id.
uint32 expected_fault_id
---
bool success
# The reason that was latched when the request was judged, or 0 (none).
uint8 reason
# Human-readable outcome: what was cleared, or why nothing was.
string message
